=== MDV-P5-031
title: Mobile ADR and threat model: two Expo store apps (Medvya Clinic, Medvya for patients) from one repo
type: Spike
epic: MDV-P5-E08
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Founder, Developer
labels: mobile, adr, security
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 26-27

confidence: 80 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Mobile.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp); docs/03-architecture/frontend-architecture.md (portability)
desc:
Record ADR-011: native apps with Expo, two store apps (staff app for doctors and front desk; patient app in indigo) in a `mobile/` pnpm workspace sharing tokens, i18n messages, API contracts and `domain/` + `services/` code with `web/`. Decide token auth for native clients (OIDC code + PKCE with secure-store; the web BFF cookie is not reused), what may be stored on the device (nothing but tokens, device key and an encrypted offline queue), push payload rule, EAS Update scope, and the store-account owner. Update the data map and threat model for devices.
ac:
- Given the ADR, when it is accepted, then it names the two apps, the repo folders, the auth flow and the on-device storage rule.
- Given the threat model, when it is reviewed, then lost phone, shared phone, screenshot, push preview and offline queue each have a control.
- Given the data map, when it is updated, then device storage and push payloads are listed with their classification.

=== MDV-P5-032
title: Mobile foundation: `mobile/` Expo workspace, shared tokens and i18n, RTL, CI and EAS builds
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E08
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Developer
labels: mobile, platform
estimate: 4
weeks: 28-29
depends: MDV-P5-031
confidence: 70 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Mobile.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp); packages/ui tokens; packages/i18n
desc:
Create `mobile/clinician` and `mobile/patient` (expo-router, bottom sheets, secure-store, encrypted expo-sqlite, expo-localization with forceRTL for Arabic, Dynamic Type to 200 %). One tokens file feeds web CSS variables and the native theme (clinic teal, patient indigo). Reuse `packages/i18n/messages` (en, hi, ar). Lint layer rules as ADR-009 (`domain`, `services`, `hooks`, `components`). CI: type-check, unit tests, EAS preview builds, `pnpm audit`.
ac:
- Given the workspace, when CI runs, then both apps type-check, lint, test and produce an EAS preview build.
- Given Arabic is selected, when the app restarts, then layout is right-to-left while dates and phone numbers stay left-to-right.
- Given a string is hard-coded in a component, when lint runs, then the build fails.
- Given the tokens file changes, when web and native build, then both pick up the same colours and spacing.

=== MDV-P5-033
title: Mobile backend: native token sign-in, device registry, push registry and remote revoke
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E08
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Developer, Security
labels: mobile, auth, security
estimate: 3.5
weeks: 28-30
depends: MDV-P5-031, MDV-P0-011
confidence: 70 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Mobile.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp); MDV-P0-011/012/013
desc:
Server side for native clients: OIDC code + PKCE token endpoints, refresh rotation, patient sign-in by mobile number + SMS code, device registration (device key, platform, app version), push token registry, per-device and all-device revoke (feeds the 'My devices' screen and staff offboarding MDV-P1-009), rate limits and audit. Every endpoint declares a policy; tenant isolation unchanged.
ac:
- Given a staff member is offboarded, when the owner confirms, then every mobile session and push token of that person is revoked at once.
- Given a refresh token is replayed, when the server sees it twice, then the whole token family is revoked and the event is audited.
- Given a wrong SMS code is entered five times, when the limit is reached, then the number is locked for a period and the patient is told in plain words.
- Given a lost phone is reported, when the user revokes it in My devices, then the next request from that device is refused.

=== MDV-P5-034
title: Staff app: sign-in, 15-minute biometric lock, Today, queue, patient search and patient summary
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E08
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Receptionist, Nurse
labels: mobile, staff-app
estimate: 4
weeks: 29-31
depends: MDV-P5-032, MDV-P5-033, MDV-P2-001
confidence: 65 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Mobile.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (staff app); MDV-P2-001 Today; MDV-P1-001 queue
desc:
Staff app: work email + passkey or code, choose facility, Face ID / fingerprint unlock after a 15-minute lock with PIN fallback and switch user, Today with next patient hero, queue with tokens and 'via app' marks, privacy-safe patient search, patient summary (allergy never by colour alone), offline banner with read-only last copy, role-based tabs (5 maximum). Same capabilities and care-relationship rules as the web app, enforced by the API.
ac:
- Given the app is idle for 15 minutes, when it is opened again, then it asks for Face ID, fingerprint or PIN before showing anything.
- Given a receptionist signs in, when the tabs load, then clinical-only tabs are absent and their API calls return 403.
- Given the phone is offline, when the doctor opens Today, then the last copy shows with an offline banner and no edit action.
- Given a patient has an allergy, when the summary opens, then the allergy shows as text and icon, not colour alone.
- Given the staff app is open, when someone takes a screenshot, then Android blocks it and iOS blurs the app switcher and audits the screenshot (ADR-011 §6).
- Given the phone is revoked or the user switches, when the app next talks to the server, then the encrypted store is wiped and nothing of the previous user remains (ADR-011 §3, §5).

=== MDV-P5-035
title: Staff app: consent script, background recording with offline queue, AI note review and sign
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E08
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: mobile, staff-app, ai-scribe
estimate: 5
weeks: 31-33
depends: MDV-P5-034, MDV-P3-001
confidence: 50 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Mobile.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (consultation); MDV-P3 AI scribe tickets
desc:
Consult flow on the phone: ask-first consent script (agree / decline to manual note), recording with a visible indicator and background audio, chunk upload with retry and an encrypted offline queue, draft note with per-field accept, sign with biometrics. AI output stays a draft until the licensed doctor accepts each field and signs. Prescribing stays on the web app at launch (the design says so).
ac:
- Given the doctor declines recording, when the patient says no, then the app opens the manual note and records nothing.
- Given the network drops mid-recording, when it returns, then queued chunks upload in order and none is lost or duplicated.
- Given an AI draft field, when the doctor has not accepted it, then the note cannot be signed.
- Given the phone is lost, when the queue held audio, then it is encrypted and removed on remote revoke.
- Given unsent audio was wiped by a revoke, when the visit is opened on the web, then it is flagged 'recording incomplete: write the note by hand' (ADR-011 §4).

=== MDV-P5-036
title: Patient app: SMS sign-in, family profiles, home, booking, check-in and reschedule
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E08
prd: P8-06, P4-07
screens: R-01, R-02
priority: MUST
roles: Patient, Caregiver
labels: mobile, patient-app
estimate: 5
weeks: 29-32
depends: MDV-P5-032, MDV-P5-033, MDV-P4-020, MDV-P4-023
confidence: 65 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Mobile.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (patient app); R-01, R-02, R-04
desc:
Patient app (indigo): mobile number + SMS code (iOS one-time-code autofill, Android SMS Retriever), then biometric or PIN; 'who is this for' with family profiles and proxy access that is explicit, time-limited and visible; home with next visit, to-do list and emergency line; book (doctor, visit type, date, time, fee line), confirmation with add-to-calendar, check-in and reschedule; last copy offline, bookings queued. Same booking service and no-double-booking rule as reception.
ac:
- Given a patient books from the app, when a reception booking takes the same slot, then only one succeeds and the other sees the next free slots.
- Given a family member is viewed, when the proxy has expired, then access ends and the patient sees why.
- Given the phone is offline, when the patient books, then the booking is queued and shown as not yet confirmed.
- Given the SMS code arrives, when the patient opens the app, then the code is filled in automatically on iOS and Android.
- Given a rooted or jailbroken phone, when the patient app starts, then it warns and keeps working; the staff app refuses to sign in (ADR-011 §7).

=== MDV-P5-037
title: Patient app: results, prescriptions, messages, consents, payments and video visit
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E08
prd: P8-06, P4-07
screens: R-01, R-03
priority: MUST
roles: Patient
labels: mobile, patient-app, payments
estimate: 5
weeks: 31-34
depends: MDV-P5-036, MDV-P4-007
confidence: 55 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Mobile.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (patient app, pay, video visit)
desc:
Records the patient may see (signed summaries and reviewed results only, plain words, never AI drafts), prescriptions with QR, clinic messages (with the 'not for emergencies' rule), consents and family access, payment sheet (UPI, cards; Apple Pay in UAE) marked paid only when the bank or gateway confirms, receipts to Records and WhatsApp, and the video-visit join screen (camera and microphone check). Video joins only when teleconsultation (MDV-P8-002) is switched on for the clinic; until then the entry is hidden by flag.
ac:
- Given a result is not reviewed, when the patient opens Records, then it shows as pending, not as a value.
- Given a payment, when the bank has not confirmed, then the invoice is not marked paid.
- Given a draft AI note exists, when the patient opens Records, then nothing of it is visible.
- Given video visits are not enabled for the clinic, when the patient opens the app, then no video entry is shown.

=== MDV-P5-038
title: Private push notifications for both apps (IDs only, no health text on the lock screen)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E08
