sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Mobile.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (mobile rules)
desc:
APNs and FCM through Azure Notification Hubs in the tenant's country. Payloads carry an opaque ID and the fixed text 'You have an update from your clinic'; the app fetches the detail after unlock. Per-user opt-in and quiet hours; failures visible in the staff notification centre (MDV-P1-034).
ac:
- Given a result is ready, when a push is sent, then the payload holds an ID and the fixed text and no test, doctor speciality or result.
- Given the user turns notifications off, when an event happens, then no push is sent and the in-app list still shows it.
- Given a push token is revoked, when an event happens, then no push goes to that device.

