=== MDV-P5-040
title: Platform console shell (`web/platform-admin`): company sign-on plus security key, platform roles, reason on every action, no PHI
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-08
screens: N-12
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Founder
labels: platform, admin, security
estimate: 4
weeks: 26-28
depends: MDV-P0-011
confidence: 65 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (sign-in, overview, team access, audit log)
desc:
Separate app and host for the Medvya team: company SSO then a security key (no passwords, no shared accounts), lost-key recovery by a second owner with a one-hour link, roles (owner, operations, support, finance, reviewer), quarterly access review, nav of 16 pages, every action needs a reason and is logged to an append-only platform audit log that can be exported. The console reads only the control plane: tenant catalogue, plan, routing and counts; it never shows patient records (data map and architecture test).
ac:
- Given a Medvya user, when signs in without a security key, then access is refused.
- Given a platform action, when is taken without a reason, then it is rejected.
- Given any console endpoint, when returns data, then it holds no patient field (architecture test).
- Given a key is lost, when another owner verifies on a video call, then a one-hour link is issued, the old key is revoked and both steps are logged.

=== MDV-P5-041
title: Feature rollouts: staged release (internal, beta tenants, percentage, everyone), kill switch and clinical sign-off gate
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-08
screens: N-12
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations
labels: platform, flags
