sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Features and rollouts); MDV-P0-028
desc:
Extends the per-tenant flags (MDV-P0-028) with stages and a percentage, owner and description, and a one-click 'turn off for all' that hides a feature without deleting data. A clinical feature (recording, AI notes, e-prescriptions) cannot reach 'everyone' until clinical sign-off is recorded. Plans decide who is entitled; flags decide what is on.
ac:
- Given a clinical flag, when is moved to everyone without sign-off, then the change is refused.
- Given the kill switch, when is used, then the feature disappears for all tenants and no data is deleted.
- Given a flag change, when is made, then it is audited with a reason.

=== MDV-P5-042
title: Plans and entitlements: versioned plans, India and UAE prices, seats, trial days, 30 days' notice
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-07
screens: N-11
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Finance
labels: platform, billing
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 26-28
depends: MDV-P5-016, MDV-P5-040
confidence: 70 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Plans); docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (pricing 06 Nov 2026)
desc:
Plans (Clinic with one doctor ₹1,999 per month; Clinic ₹3,499 per doctor per month; Hospital custom) with separate INR and AED prices, seats, trial days and the feature list. An edit creates a new plan version: new subscriptions use it now, existing ones at renewal with 30 days' notice. Removing a feature never deletes data. Entitlements are read by the feature gate.
ac:
- Given a plan is edited, when it is saved, then a new version exists and current subscribers keep the old one until renewal.
- Given a price changes, when a subscriber exists, then they are notified 30 days before it applies.
- Given a feature is removed from a plan, when data exists, then the data stays.
notes:
- The "Solo" plan is a one-doctor Clinic plan, not an individual account (ADR-016 (docs/adr/ADR-016-organisation-onboarding-and-approval.md, owner decision 10 Nov 2026)); revisit plan names and seat types (doctors, staff, patients) when this is built. This ticket replaces the hard-coded starter plan (1 doctor and 2 staff, patients uncapped) enforced from MDV-P1-069, and adds the owner's self-service upgrade.
- Seat counts are per organisation in total across its locations (ADR-016, MDV-P1-069); bigger chains need a bigger plan.

=== MDV-P5-043
title: Subscription billing in the console and for owners: invoices, payment method, add seats, dunning ladder, close practice
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-07
screens: N-11
priority: MUST
roles: Practice owner, Medvya operations
labels: platform, billing
estimate: 3.5
weeks: 27-29
depends: MDV-P5-016, MDV-P5-040
confidence: 60 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Subscription billing); docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (owner Billing, Close this practice)
desc:
Owner screens: plan and seats, invoices from Medvya, update payment method, add seats, close the practice (full export first). Console: INR and AED reported separately, never summed. Dunning: retries day 3 and 7, reminder day 14, limited mode day 30 (online bookings pause), read-only day 60, suspended day 90; patients and clinical records are never locked for non-payment. Only the owner sees plan and billing.
ac:
- Given a payment fails, when day 30 is reached, then online bookings pause and clinicians can still read and treat.
- Given a non-owner, when opens billing, then the API returns 403.
- Given a practice is closed, when the owner confirms, then a full export is offered first and the plan stops at the end of the paid period.

