depends: MDV-P5-040, MDV-P1-064, MDV-P2-023
confidence: 65 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/adr/ADR-016-organisation-onboarding-and-approval.md; docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Doctor licence verification, to be redrawn as organisation review)
desc:
Superseded scope (ADR-016): the reviewer queue lists organisation onboarding requests (type Clinic or Hospital, country, submitted date, documents, state), not doctors. The reviewer opens the uploaded documents, then approves, asks for changes with a plain reason, rejects with a reason, or later suspends an approved organisation. The queue reads only the control-plane request and documents through its own narrow, reviewed read path (ADR-014), never patient data. Extends the simple queue and documented API built in MDV-P1-064 (documents view, suspension, reviewer roles). The design file still shows the doctor-licence screen and must be redrawn.
ac:
- Given an organisation is Submitted, when a reviewer approves it, then reviewer, documents checked and time are recorded and the organisation can register patients.
- Given a reviewer asks for changes or rejects, when it is saved, then the applicant gets the reason in plain words by email and on the status page.
- Given an organisation is suspended, when staff sign in, then new registration, booking and signing are refused and existing records stay readable for care.
- Given any queue endpoint, when it returns data, then it holds no patient field (architecture test); every action needs a reason.

=== MDV-P5-045
title: Releases and What's new, maintenance and incident banners, integrations register
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-09
screens: N-13
priority: SHOULD
roles: Medvya operations
labels: platform, status, comms
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 29-31
depends: MDV-P5-040, MDV-P5-041
confidence: 65 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Releases, Status and maintenance, Integrations)
desc:
Announcements linked to a flag and shown when the flag reaches the tenant (in-app What's new, owner email, never to patients). Planned maintenance and incident messages per region as banners in the clinic app and on the public status page (MDV-P5-018). Integrations register per country (NHCX, DHA eClaimLink, Shafafiya, Riayati, payment gateways, ABDM, WhatsApp) with status, read-only.
ac:
- Given a flag reaches a tenant, when an announcement is linked, then it shows in What's new only then.
- Given maintenance is scheduled for India, when the time comes, then only India practices see the banner.
- Given the register, when is opened, then it shows each integration's status and country.

=== MDV-P5-046
title: Legal documents: versioned terms, privacy notice and DPA, re-acceptance gate that pauses booking only
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-08
screens: N-12
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Counsel, Practice owner
labels: platform, legal, consent
estimate: 2
weeks: 27-29
depends: MDV-P5-040, MDV-P1-044
confidence: 65 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Legal documents and acceptance)
desc:
Counsel writes the wording and uploads it; staff can only publish an approved version, never edit text. A new version can require every owner to accept again; until they do only online booking pauses, nothing clinical stops (the existing terms gate is reused). Acceptance is recorded with who, version and time.
ac:
- Given a new version requires acceptance, when an owner has not accepted, then online booking pauses and clinical work continues.
- Given platform staff, when try to edit wording, then the console offers no edit, only publish.
- Given an owner accepts, when it is saved, then user, version and time are recorded.

=== MDV-P5-047
title: Service requests: Help in the clinic app, support inbox with SLA, internal notes, diagnostics
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-09
screens: N-13
priority: MUST
roles: Practice owner, Medvya support
labels: platform, support
estimate: 3.5
weeks: 28-30
depends: MDV-P5-040, MDV-P5-018
confidence: 65 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Service requests); docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Raise a service request)
desc:
Clinic side: search help first, raise a request with category and description, warning not to include patient details, screenshots blurred where patient data appears, app version and recent errors attached. Console side: inbox with SLA timer, assignee, public replies and internal notes, 'request support access' that needs the owner's approval, lasts 60 minutes and shows no patient records. Support hours and urgent-outage line shown.
ac:
- Given a screenshot shows patient data, when it is attached, then the patient data is blurred before storage.
- Given support, when asks for access, then nothing is visible until the owner approves and it ends after 60 minutes.
- Given a request breaches its SLA, when time passes, then it is flagged to the team lead.

=== MDV-P5-048
title: Platform analytics, practice health score and scheduled reports with small-count hiding
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-08
screens: N-12
priority: SHOULD
roles: Medvya operations, Founder
labels: platform, analytics
estimate: 3.5
weeks: 30-32
depends: MDV-P5-040, MDV-P4-029
confidence: 55 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Analytics, Practices at risk, Reports)
desc:
Aggregated adoption and usage by practice, staff and patients with no patient data; any count under 5 is hidden. Health score from usage, payments, support tickets and errors, with a reason and a next step. Reports (metrics, daily/weekly/monthly, PDF or CSV) sent to named people only. Reuses the PHI-free reporting store decided in MDV-P4-029.
ac:
- Given a count is 4, when the chart renders, then it shows as hidden.
- Given a report, when is scheduled, then only the named recipients get it and it holds no patient data.
- Given a practice's health score falls, when it is shown, then the reasons are listed.

=== MDV-P5-049
title: Data requests and offboarding runs from the console without opening records
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-09
screens: N-14
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Practice owner
labels: platform, privacy, offboarding
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 29-31
depends: MDV-P5-040, MDV-P5-019, MDV-P5-025
confidence: 65 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Admin.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Data requests and offboarding)
desc:
Queue of export, correction, erasure and practice-closure requests from owners. Closure: full export first, records kept under a hold for the legal retention period, then deleted with a certificate; region never changes. Operations run the jobs and see counts and status only, never records.
ac:
- Given a closure is requested, when it is approved, then a full export is delivered before any retention clock starts.
- Given retention ends, when the job runs, then records are deleted and a certificate is stored.
- Given an operator, when opens a request, then no record content is shown.

=== MDV-P5-050
title: Public pricing page with 14-day trial, monthly and yearly toggle and country currency
type: Story
epic: MDV-P5-E09
prd: P5-07
screens: F-01
priority: SHOULD
roles: Public, Practice owner
labels: public-site, billing
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 26-27
depends: MDV-P5-042, MDV-P1-027
confidence: 75 | Design exists (6 Nov 2026); build estimate not yet calibrated.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (Simple plans, 14-day free trial)
desc:
Pricing page on the public site reading the approved plans (MDV-P5-042): Solo, Clinic (most popular), Hospital (talk to us), monthly and yearly toggle with the yearly saving, ₹ or AED by region, 'prices approved' line, payment methods by country. 'Start free trial' goes to sign-up (MDV-P1-004) with the plan chosen. No card needed to start unless the pricing decision says otherwise. Also the 6 Nov blocks: Compare plans table (Solo, Clinic, Hospital), the Medvya Assist add-on per doctor, "If a payment fails" (nothing locks for 30 days; records are never locked and can always be exported) and free migration. Until the console plans exist (MDV-P5-042), the approved plans are read from a versioned file in PublicSite (like trust-centre.json), recorded as a shortcut.
ac:
- Given a visitor in the UAE, when opens pricing, then prices show in AED with Apple Pay and cards listed.
- Given a visitor, when chooses Clinic and starts a trial, then sign-up opens with that plan.
- Given a price changes in the console, when the page reloads, then the new price shows.
- Given JavaScript is off, when the monthly or yearly choice is made, then the prices switch (plain links or a form, no script); axe is clean in en, hi and ar.
